# Akam release signing keys, in the ssh-keygen allowed_signers format.
#
# PLACEHOLDER: no maintainer key has been published yet, so no signature can be
# authenticated and tools/release/verify_kit.sh refuses a signed kit (an
# unsigned kit needs --allow-unsigned).
#
# The maintainer adds ONE line per public key, below this comment:
#
#   akam-release namespaces="akam-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...base64... maintainer@example
#
# Get the key text with:  cat ~/.ssh/akam_release.pub   (starts with "ssh-ed25519 AAAA...")
# The principal must stay "akam-release" and so must the namespace.
# The same public key must also be quoted in README.md and in the release notes,
# so that it can be cross-checked from another channel. Never put a private key here.
